  "id": "affect-misattribution-procedure",
  "term": "affect misattribution procedure",
  "definition": "An affect misattribution procedure is a computer-administered sequential priming assessment used to estimate implicit attitudes or stigma. In this packet, it is described as an alternative to deliberate self-report for measuring implicit internalized sexual orientation stigma.",
